/E (The Goal )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
546 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (The primary objective of Activity One is a test of pure mechanical efficiency and stability. Teams are challenged to navigate their crawler bot across the full length of the 8-meter competition rope from Point A to Point B. While the task involves reaching the finish line as quickly as possible, the environment is designed to simulate the unpredictability of real-world infrastructure. Robots must endure intentional disturbances, including tension variations, and controlled vibrations. This activity serves as the ultimate stress test for the robustness of the crawler mechanism, exposing any weaknesses in grip strategy, chassis balance, and power management.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
547 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (Race Procedure )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
548 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
549 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (Checkpoints and Recovery Protocol )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
550 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (To balance difficulty with competitive fairness, fixed checkpoints are established at predetermined intervals along the rope. These serve as "save points" to prevent a single error from ending a team's run entirely.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
551 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (The Fall Rule: If a robot loses its grip and slips off the rope, the run is not reset to zero. Instead, the team is permitted to manually retrieve the bot and reattach it at the last checkpoint successfully passed.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
552 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (Time Penalty: The clock does not stop during this recovery process. Therefore, a fall naturally incurs a time penalty, as the team loses valuable seconds retrieving and resetting the bot.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
553 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (Timing System and Transparency )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
554 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (To ensure absolute fairness and accuracy, the timing process is strictly governed by a dual-verification system:)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
555 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (Live Stopwatch: A large, visible digital stopwatch will run live during the attempt, allowing the audience and teams to track progress in real-time.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
556 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (Hand Stopwatch: A designated official timekeeper will simultaneously operate a high-precision handheld stopwatch to cross-check the live time. The final recorded time will be verified against both devices. In the event of a close call or dispute, a video camera recording at 60fps or higher will serve as the official reference, ensuring that every team has equal assurance of accuracy regarding start and stop times.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
