/E (\(1920X1080p\) showing the robot in motion. The video must unequivocally demonstrate that the bot is hanging from the rope and traversing it using the correct crawling or grip-and-pull mechanism, and that it does not use wheels to drive along the rope length. In addition, the robot must be shown meeting the key build rules, including proper rope safety, battery-only operation, and correct start configuration dimensions. The guide for this screening phase makes it clear that any failure in the compliance check can result in immediate disqualification or a requirement to re-engineer before final selection, and that the top spots go to teams that demonstrate the most reliable locomotion, strict adherence to safety/design rules, and robust build quality during screening.)
